---
title: Sequence diagram - silent token refresh after a 401 (web lib/api.js; mobile ApiClient Authenticator works the same way)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as Web portal<br/>lib/api.js
    participant AC as AuthController
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant RT as InMemoryRefreshTokenStore

    W->>AC: any API call with an expired access token
    AC-->>W: 401 (JWT bearer: lifetime check, no clock skew)
    W->>AC: POST /api/auth/refresh {refreshToken} (once per request, concurrent calls share one refresh)
    alt refresh token missing
        AC-->>W: 400 "Refresh token is required."
    else
        AC->>AS: RefreshTokenAsync(token)
        AS->>RT: GetTokenAsync(token)
        alt token unknown, revoked, expired, or user inactive
            AS-->>AC: null
            AC-->>W: 401 "Refresh token is invalid or has expired."
            W-->>U: /#35;/login with "session expired", return to the page afterwards
        else token active
            AS->>RT: RevokeTokenAsync(old, replacedBy new)
            AS->>RT: SaveTokenAsync(new, 7 days)
            AS-->>AC: AuthResponse
            AC-->>W: 200 new access + refresh token
            W->>AC: retry the original request with the new access token
        end
    end
    Note over RT: Tokens live in API memory: an API restart signs everyone out
